# Python AWS Static Website Deployment

## 📌 Project Overview

This project demonstrates how to deploy a static website on **Amazon S3 using Python and Boto3**.

The Python script automates the process of creating an S3 bucket, enabling static website hosting, configuring public read access, and uploading website files.

## 🎯 Objectives

- Learn Python functions and libraries.
- Understand AWS automation using Boto3.
- Create and configure an Amazon S3 bucket.
- Upload static website files to AWS.
- Access the deployed website using an S3 website endpoint.
- Practise Git and GitHub for version control.

## 🏗️ Architecture

```text
Developer
    |
    v
Python Script (deploy.py)
    |
    v
Boto3 AWS SDK
    |
    v
Amazon S3 Bucket
    |
    v
Static Website
(HTML, CSS, JavaScript)
    |
    v
Web Browser
```

## 🛠️ Technologies Used

- **Python** – Automation scripting
- **Boto3** – AWS SDK for Python
- **Amazon S3** – Static website hosting and file storage
- **AWS CLI** – AWS credential configuration
- **Git** – Version control
- **GitHub** – Source code repository

